{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793656756,"nonce":"CMrWGsxs633fBw1Sr/5fm7xc3vQ=","message":"Shared-history foundation implemented in b647bb241ff3ad74c3aa7fa097e0e5d3dacba73a.\n\nThe pure Rust engine deterministically seeds a Yrs history from workspace/path/published generation. Independent UTF-16 replicas converge without duplicate seed text; concurrent updates and deletions exchange against the accepted frontier. Retried updates are idempotent. Lineage changes, unknown dependencies, seed-client clock changes, invalid encodings and impossible vector counts are refused before altering the acknowledged graph. Vectors compare by their decoded contents, not byte order.\n\nThe existing workspace Durable Object now supports owner/workspace-capability scoped documents/open and documents/exchange. It persists checksummed incremental segments, metadata and quota in one bulk commit before replying. Compaction runs after 64 segments or 256 KiB of deltas; idle objects hold no loaded graphs. Bounds: 1 MiB text/4 MiB encoded history per document, 64 MiB workspace payload and 256 path slots including retired paths. Payloads count against both workspace and account allowances. The native Rust document client and example driver interoperate with the real local Rust Worker.\n\nSnapshot publication is serialized with exchanges. Unchanged saved files retain pending shared heads; publishing the exact head integrates it without reseeding history. Replacing/deleting pending shared text is refused. Replacing a clean file retires its lineage and clears payloads; recreation receives a fresh lineage, so old replicas cannot write into it. Retired path slots remain bounded metadata; unbounded retirement/garbage collection is not advertised.\n\nVerification: 100 engine tests; 41 Worker tests including 8 shared-history cases; independent clients, Unicode/concurrent/deletion-only edits, duplicate delivery, missing dependencies, owner/capability isolation, snapshot fencing/integration/recreation, compaction and a fresh gateway instance, quota refusal, corrupted durable chunks and injected storage failure. Corruption/failure preserve the last acknowledged graph/sequence/quota and recover after storage is restored. The failed-write fixture deliberately injects a rejected trigger into its stopped private SQLite database; workerd diagnostic errors in that case are expected. Native session, runner and RayScript dependency checks pass. Rebuilt Rust Worker, optimized session and editor WASM; browser smoke covers live editing/reload persistence, mobile fallback and nested modules. The editor bundle is byte-identical, so no generated artifact commit is needed.\n\nThis closes only the shared-history/exchange prerequisite. Automatic editor binding/migration is e254e27e1f2ce280813c42a71ca590739ad8aa8d091c4598e5f4cae9811c483f. Pushed delivery with bounded reconnect/hibernation is 87a7cd157e91265a33566edeed409b32e26e47d3a1bcf8840a57e0d14907bcf6. Existing independently initialized session graphs must not be attached blindly. The UI still uses saved-file sync actions until those integrations are implemented and verified. Production Cloudflare/MSB deployment validation remains separate; this milestone needed no external deployment or secrets.","files":null}]}